this road leads right into the war the  intersection near Pope asthma is scarred  by the heavy fighting it has witnessed  the OSCE mission regularly sends  observers to note any breaches of the  Minsk agreement but this morning things  are relatively quiet Ukrainian soldiers  take us to the frontline this unit has  been stationed in a forest near Pope  Asma for six weeks now the commander  says he's glad they haven't lost any men  yet just across from them no-man's land  this so-called gray zone is a  demilitarized area but despite its name  shots continued to be fired at Ukrainian  soldiers the room hear the sound of  gunfire echoes across the frozen fields  the platoon leader calls this front  music he says the separatists aren't  observing the ceasefire the other side  is trying to provoke us so that we open  fire at them but we stay still and they  shoot the OSCE says the Ukrainians have  also been breaking the ceasefire but the  military denies this only when the life  or well-being of our soldiers is in  danger that's when we give the orders to  fire but if this is the case we only use  weapons allowed by the Minsk agreement  on this day the Ukrainian military has  already counted 37 violations of the  ceasefire the independent OSCE report is  not yet available for eastern Ukraine  this is the third winter at war all  efforts to revitalize the so-called  minced peace process ended in a deadlock  Ukraine and Russian backed separatists  cannot agree upon a roadmap how to bring  peace to the embattled region for the  soldiers in the trenches this is a  static battle in a frozen conflict
 

